  "limitations": [
    "TRUYN/2 in selection examples is synthetic input exercising the selection algorithm; it does not advertise a deployed TRUYN/2 implementation.",
    "The current helper accepts flat semantic lists, not per-generation semantic maps. Multi-generation capability claims must not be inferred from these cases; that extension needs separate representation and conformance.",
    "The pure negotiation helper normalizes string arrays, while authenticated registration and peer-session boundaries explicitly validate advertisement shape before issuing authority.",
    "Compatibility selection is not authorization, descriptor trust, provider visibility, billing entitlement, signature validation, or stable release qualification."
  ]
